{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Remember</b> — this verse is the seventh verse and begins with seven, because the Sabbath is seventh, and seven are mentioned in the verse: you, your son, your daughter, your servant, your maid, your beast, and your stranger. Corresponding to them they established seven rests in 'You shall not do any work.' And the verse 'Remember' has five words, to tell you: whoever fulfills the Sabbath is as if he fulfilled the Five Books of the Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:42.690108998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}